, single channel procedure</article-title><source><italic>Surgical Endoscopy</italic></source><year>2012</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>523</fpage><lpage>527</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">21938576</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ein</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Langer</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Daneman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nonoperative management of pediatric ruptured appendix with inflammatory mass or abscess: presence of an appendicolith predicts recurrent appendicitis</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Pediatric Surgery</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>40</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>1612</fpage><lpage>1615</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="other">2-s2.0-27444442786</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16226993</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Yaghoubian</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaji</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Laparoscopic vs open appendectomy in children.Outcomes comparison based on age, sex and perforation status</article-title><source><italic>Archives of Surgery</italic></source><year>2011</year><volume>146</volume><fpage>1118</fpage><lpage>1121</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">21690438</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stylianos</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Nichols</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Ventura</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name